  "html_source": "<p>20 quid = £20 = pound sterling. The term  “quid” is British slang (still widely in use) for £1 in currency, which is also the official currency of the United Kingdom. Ireland <a href=\"https://www.google.co.uk/search?q=when+did+ireland+adopt+the+euro&amp;oq=when+did+ireland+adopt+the+euro&amp;aqs=chrome..69i57j0l5.6143j0j4&amp;sourceid=chrome&amp;ie=UTF-8\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\">adopted the Euro</a> in 2002.</p><p><img src=\"https://images.rapgenius.com/767vzvzdqhkv4fgpsv69dahyx.640x361x1.jpg\" alt=\"\" /></p>",
